            "relation": "USES_PHYSICAL_SCHEME",
            "target_entity_instance": "two-dimensional diffusive wave model",
            "target_entity_type": "PhysicalScheme",
            "paragraph": "This study utilized a rainfall-runoff-inundation (RRI) model coupled with a reservoir operation model to quantify to effect of climate change on hydropower generation (Sayama et al., 2012). The fully distributed RRI model is capable of calculating both runoff and inundation concurrently. This model employed a two-dimensional diffusive wave model to determine the hydrological process in the slope, while one-dimensional model was adopted to describe channel flow.",
